'''Badweyn''' (Burawi: ''Badweyn'', meaning "Big Ocean"), officially the '''Badweyn Rural Administration''', is a [[Administrative divisions of Burawa|rural administration]] in the [[Dafar]] cultural region of western [[Burawa]]. With an area of 3,594.605 km² and a population of 380,000 as of 2024, it is characterised by its coastal geography and distinctive political culture.

The administration is bordered by [[Dafar Hoose Rural Administration|Dafar Hoose]] to the north, with the [[Aethiopean Ocean]] surrounding it on all other sides. The seat of government is the town of [[Badweyn (town)|Badweyn]].

== Geography ==

Badweyn occupies a coastal peninsula in the southern portion of the [[Dafar]] region. The terrain consists of coastal plains and rolling agricultural land. The administration is nearly surrounded by the [[Aethiopean Ocean]], with only its northern boundary connecting to the mainland.

The coastal location provides access to fishing grounds and maritime trade routes, contributing to the regional economy. The climate is {{w|humid subtropical}}, moderated by oceanic influences.

